725	The fact that the strategy wins the game with probability $1$ is proven as Proposition \ref{prop: perfect strategy}. The special case of $\e=0$ is the main result of \S \ref{subsection:exact-self-testing}. We remark that although the robustness bound does not seem to depend directly on $n$, typically $\Delta$ does.
